<article class="env-lemma" id="0C6M">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C6M">Lemma <span data-tag="0C6M">53.10.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a proper curve over a field $k$ with $H^0(X, \mathcal{O}_ X) = k$. If $X$ has genus $0$, then every invertible $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module $\mathcal{L}$ of degree $0$ is trivial. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Namely, we have $\dim _ k H^0(X, \mathcal{L}) \geq 0 + 1 - 0 = 1$ by Riemann-Roch (Lemma <a href="/tag/0BS6" data-tag="0BS6">53.5.2</a>), hence $\mathcal{L}$ has a nonzero section, hence $\mathcal{L} \cong \mathcal{O}_ X$ by Varieties, Lemma <a href="/tag/0B40" data-tag="0B40">33.44.12</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>